  "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
  "instance_name": "racial_justification_of_death",
  "label": "The act of justifying death based on racial stereotypes or prejudices",
  "description": "Racial justification of death refers to the act of justifying death based on racial stereotypes or prejudices, often by implying that the victims are not human or that their death is not a serious issue. In the meme, the implication that killing zombies (non-human entities) is not homicide is used to justify racially motivated death. This requires understanding of the concept of racial justification of death and its role in promoting harmful ideologies.",
